msgstr "Each goal's progress is how far you have moved from its starting value toward its target, capped at 100% once reached. The total weighs each counted goal by its priority (low 1, normal 2, high 3). Paused or cancelled goals, and goals without a target, current value or direction, are left out instead of counted as zero."

#: packages/api/src/presenters/score.ts
msgid "Each input is compared with your own median over the 28 days before it (at least 7 days with data are needed). 50 means in line with your usual. More sleep than usual raises that part; a higher resting heart rate, or a heavier recent activity load than usual, lowers its part. The index is the plain average of the parts your profile uses."
msgstr "Each input is compared with your own median over the 28 days before it (at least 7 days with data are needed). 50 means in line with your usual. More sleep than usual raises that part; a higher resting heart rate, or a heavier recent activity load than usual, lowers its part. The index is the plain average of the parts your profile uses."

#: packages/api/src/presenters/insights.ts
msgid "Each rule compares your last 7 days with your own usual (the median of the 28 days before). A change is only described when it is larger than both your usual day-to-day variation and a fixed minimum size, and when most recent days sit on the same side. A new device or app starts a new usual instead of being mixed with the old one."
msgstr "Each rule compares your last 7 days with your own usual (the median of the 28 days before). A change is only described when it is larger than both your usual day-to-day variation and a fixed minimum size, and when most recent days sit on the same side. A new device or app starts a new usual instead of being mixed with the old one."

